Hi.  I received Tetris for System V off the net some time back and I, along with
may other users here have become addicted to it.  Now I have some users who have
a bunch of ideas on modifying the game and are bugging me to do it, but I have
not the know-how to do it all.  So I thought I would post the list to the net
to solicit some ideas (or patches) to do this, and also solicit more ideas for
modifying the game.

	1.  Add some new shapes, about 5 of them.
	2.  Move the Score, Level, and Rows information to the left hand
	    side of the screen underneath the Next: field.
	3.  Widen the screen to the right to cover the area where score,
	    etc. was.  Maybe a command line switch to determine size.
	4.  Add a pause key.
	5.  Add an option for the user to specify the keys to be used
	    on the command line.  Example:

			tetris -lh -rl -rj -Rk

            This would tell tetris that the move left key should be 'h',
	    the move right key should be 'l', the rotate left key should
	    be 'j', and the rotate right key should be 'k'.
	6.  A most useful feature would be a refresh key that would cause
	    the game to pause while it redraws the screen.
        7.  For some real fun, a command line switch on causing everything
	    to work opposite as it normally does.  What I mean by this is
	    that the blocks move from the bottom to the top and rows get
	    cleared going upwards.

I have already figured out how to pretty much add new shapes.  The only thing
I couldn't figure out was what "shape[].offset" was for.

I also have one slight problem with the current version that I have compiled
and am running on my 80386 running ISC UNIX V.3 (version 1.0.5).  The problem
is that when it is run on my console, the screen sometimes gets jumbled when
it clears rows from the bottom and sometimes when the long piece moves side
ways, it leaves remnants behind that don't get cleared off until another 
piece passes through that spot.  I have similar problems with other graphic
programs, so I doubt it is the software but maybe somebody has a clue?!

If anyone has any ideas on these, or most especially, knowledge on how to do 
any of these, please contact me.  When, and if, all these changes get done I
will make sure to post the diffs, or the source if needbe, to the appropriate
groups for all to enjoy.

